{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "3CgxRnczXR", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-29", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 919479, "segment_id": "GZn7AM5xEZ", "segment_broadcast_id": "3CgxRnczXR", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction Brian Williams (New York)", "segment_description": null, "segment_duration": 50, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 919479, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "3CgxRnczXR", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-29", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 919479, "segment_id": "Sv0n9W7vaq", "segment_broadcast_id": "3CgxRnczXR", "segment_title": "Economy: Bailout Bill / House Vote", "segment_description": "(Studio: Brian Williams) The House defeat of the administration's economic bailout plan and the resulting stock market drop noted.  \n\n(Capitol: Tom Costello) The vote in the House reviewed; stock market graph shown. [Representative John BOEHNER&#134;- says vote yes.] [Representatives Adam PUTNAM&#134;, Paul KANJORSKI&#134;- support the bill.] [Representatives Mike PENCE&#134;, Louie GOHMERT&#134;- oppose the bill.] [Speaker of the House Nancy PELOSI \u2013 criticizes the \u201canything goes\u201d ideology.] [Representative Barney FRANK \u2013 states Pelosi decided to punish the country.] [Later, PELOSI \u2013 speaks of cooperation.] [President BUSH \u2013 says we continue to address this head-on.] [Treasury Secretary Henry PAULSON&#134;- says we need it as soon as possible.] The nationalization of European banks Commerce and Fortis and the sale of most of Wachovia\u2019s assets to Citigroup noted.  \n\n(Studio: Brian Williams) Report introduced.  \n\n(Chicago: Kevin Tibbles) Public opposition to the bailout bill featured; clips played from talk radio shows, including KLSX in Los Angeles and KTBB in Tyler, Texas; scenes shown of protests on Wall Street in New York City. [In Wichita, Los Angeles, Miami and Chicago, 4 PEOPLE \u2013 react.] [\u201cChicago Tribune\u201d Bruce DOLD&#134;- says all we\u2019re seeing is anger.] [Former Wall Street employee Jason NOVOTNY&#135;- explains why he came to Wall Street.]  \n\n(Studio: Brian Williams; New York Stock Exchange: Maria Bartiromo; CNBC headquarters: Steve Liesman; Washington: Chuck Todd) What happens now, the drop in the market, the political aspect of the vote and the impact on the small business owner discussed.  ", "segment_duration": 560, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63050.0", "legacy_segment_id": 919480, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "3CgxRnczXR", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-29", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 919479, "segment_id": "U0vTudhOl6", "segment_broadcast_id": "3CgxRnczXR", "segment_title": "Where They Stand (Jobs)", "segment_description": "(Studio: Brian Williams) Report introduced.  \n\n(New York: Carl Quintanilla) Where presidential candidates Senators John McCain and Barack Obama stand on jobs examined; statistics cited; details given of their positions on free trade, renewable energy projects and small business taxes. [Job seeker Jonathan WENTWORTH&#135;- says his job i